2	 * Layer 1 — Hermes executor post-hoc recovery stub.
3	 *
4	 * This stub exists so the try/finally block in index.ts can wire in recovery.
5	 * The full implementation (commit dirty tree, open draft PR, handover.md,
6	 * write blocked result.json) is delivered in T5.
7	 *
8	 * Non-throwing: every step is individually wrapped in try/catch.
9	 * Always produces a result.json — even if individual side-effects fail.
